<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  parallel_jaw_gripper.urdf.xacro — opt-in DART-compatible gripper abstraction.

  STATUS: V0 (offline geometry only). Selected via `gripper_model:=parallel_jaw`
  on ur5e_robotiq.urdf.xacro; the vendor Robotiq linkage remains the default
  (`gripper_model:=robotiq_linkage`) and is byte-for-byte unchanged by this
  file's existence. See docs/GRIPPER_REDESIGN_DESIGN.md for the full
  architecture rationale (candidate comparison, validation ladder V0-V10,
  redesigned F3 G0 concept) — this file implements only §3 (Architecture A)
  and only as far as V0 requires.

  WHY THIS EXISTS: the vendor 2F-85 model's four-bar linkage is kinematically
  fictional under this project's stack (both inner-knuckle joints are leaves;
  the coupler that would close the loop does not exist — DART rejects closed
  loops outright, confirmed by probe I-0) and its parallel-jaw property held
  only at one fixed angle after the TENTH OVERRIDE. Neither DART native mimic
  nor DART closed loops are available, and the bullet-featherstone escape is
  BLOCKED (shared-ECM mimic conflict with gz_ros2_control, doubly confirmed).
  This macro is a declared, exactly-specified 1-DOF prismatic abstraction:
  one actuated moving jaw, one fixed reference jaw, two flat pads, no mimic,
  no closed loop, no protruding collision geometry, no object-dependent
  xacro argument of any kind.

  KINEMATIC TREE (exactly two collision bodies in the whole gripper):

    parent (gripper_mount_link)
     └─ (fixed)      gripper_base_link      [NO collision]
         ├─ (fixed)      jaw_fixed_link      [NO collision]
         │   └─ (fixed)  pad_fixed_link      [BOX collision + contact sensor]
         └─ (PRISMATIC)  jaw_moving_link     [NO collision]  <- gripper_jaw_joint
             └─ (fixed)  pad_moving_link     [BOX collision + contact sensor]

  CLOSING AXIS: local +X of gripper_base_link. gripper_jaw_joint's own axis is
  "-1 0 0" (i.e. increasing q moves jaw_moving_link toward -X, toward the
  fixed jaw), so aperture is monotonically DECREASING in q, matching the
  vendor master joint's sign convention (increasing angle -> closing) even
  though the unit changes from radians to metres.

  APERTURE IDENTITY (derived below, not fitted):
    Let A0 = full-open aperture (stroke), t = pad thickness.
    jaw_fixed_link  origin (from base): x = -(A0/2 + t/2)   [rest, always]
    pad_fixed_link  origin (from jaw_fixed_link): (0,0,0)   [coincident]
      -> pad_fixed_link box, centred at x=-(A0/2+t/2), half-width t/2
      -> inner (facing +X) face at x = -A0/2                          ... (i)
    jaw_moving_link origin (from base): x = +(A0/2 + t/2), q = 0 rest
      joint axis = (-1,0,0) -> position at joint value q: x = A0/2+t/2-q
    pad_moving_link origin (from jaw_moving_link): (0,0,0) [coincident]
      -> pad_moving_link box, centred at x=A0/2+t/2-q, half-width t/2
      -> inner (facing -X) face at x = A0/2 - q                       ... (ii)
    aperture(q) = (ii) - (i) = (A0/2 - q) - (-A0/2) = A0 - q     Q.E.D.
    grasp_centre_offset(q) = midpoint of the two inner faces - x=0
                            = [(A0/2-q) + (-A0/2)] / 2 = -q/2
      i.e. magnitude q/2, direction -X = toward the fixed jaw, matching
      docs/GRIPPER_REDESIGN_DESIGN.md §3.5.

  PARALLELISM: every link above gets rpy="0 0 0" at every fixed joint, and a
  prismatic joint contributes pure translation (zero rotation) by
  construction. Therefore R(pad_moving_link) == R(pad_fixed_link) ==
  R(gripper_base_link) for ALL q — provable from the joint types alone, not
  just at a design point. This is strictly stronger than the vendor model's
  TENTH-OVERRIDE fixed-fingertip approximation, which was exact only at one
  angle.

  PAD DIMENSIONS: A0 = 0.085 m (85 mm) is carried over deliberately from the
  vendor model's own published/mesh-validated stroke (gripper_geometry.py
  validates it to 1 micron) so the aperture scale keeps its existing
  provenance. Pad height (local Z) = 0.038 m, from the vendor pad mesh's own
  measured PAD_FACE_Z_MAX_M - PAD_FACE_Z_MIN_M = 38.004 mm
  (scripts/lib/gripper_geometry.py). Pad thickness (t, local X) = 0.004 m and
  pad width (local Y) = 0.022 m are THIS FILE'S OWN CHOSEN VALUES, not
  mesh-derived — no equivalent number exists for a flat abstraction pad in the
  vendor model or the design doc, and neither figure affects the aperture,
  parallelism, or travel identities above (all purely along local X and
  independent of Y/Z box size). Flag before trusting either in a contact
  study.

  COLLISION SURFACE PARAMETERS carried over byte-identical from the vendor
  model's fingertip <surface> blocks (robotiq_2f_85_macro.urdf.xacro), so the
  mu_eff = 1.0202 friction calibration remains the applicable material result
  per docs/GRIPPER_REDESIGN_DESIGN.md §7 (contact patch changes mesh -> box,
  so a cheap re-confirmation is recommended there, not claimed here).

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, per the V0 task brief:
    - no mimic tag anywhere in this file;
    - no inner-knuckle-equivalent collision geometry (only 2 colliders exist);
    - no follower servo / no second controlled joint;
    - no fingertip_grasp_theta or any object-size-derived xacro argument;
    - visual meshes are NOT attached in this pass (cosmetic vendor-mesh
      decoration is design §8, not V0 — jaw/base links carry a plain box
      visual only, so the macro remains self-contained and inspectable).

  This file must not change the expansion of ur5e_robotiq.urdf.xacro under
  the default gripper_model:=robotiq_linkage in any way, including this
  <include>: xacro only instantiates a macro when it is invoked, so merely
  including this file's definition is inert unless
  <xacro:parallel_jaw_gripper .../> is actually called.
-->
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro" name="parallel_jaw_gripper">
    <xacro:macro name="parallel_jaw_gripper" params="
        name
        prefix
        parent
        *origin
        sim_ignition:=false
        sim_isaac:=false
        use_fake_hardware:=false
        fake_sensor_commands:=false
        include_ros2_control:=true
        aperture_m:=0.085
        pad_thickness_m:=0.004
        pad_width_m:=0.022
        pad_height_m:=0.038
        finger_standoff_z_m:=0.038
        jaw_effort:=20.0
        jaw_velocity:=0.1">

        <!-- Derived, offline, so both the URDF and this comment stay in sync
             with whatever aperture_m/pad_thickness_m the caller passes. -->
        <xacro:property name="A0" value="${aperture_m}"/>
        <xacro:property name="T"  value="${pad_thickness_m}"/>
        <xacro:property name="LZ" value="${finger_standoff_z_m}"/>
        <xacro:property name="FIXED_JAW_X"  value="${-(A0/2.0 + T/2.0)}"/>
        <xacro:property name="MOVING_JAW_X0" value="${A0/2.0 + T/2.0}"/>

        <!-- ================================================================= -->
        <!-- ros2_control — one actuated prismatic joint, self-contained       -->
        <!-- (does not touch vendor/robotiq_gripper.ros2_control.xacro).       -->
        <!-- Interface shape mirrors the vendor master joint's, per            -->
        <!-- docs/GRIPPER_REDESIGN_DESIGN.md §3.9, so gripper_close_and_hold() -->
        <!-- and the stall/GripperCommand machinery keep their expected shape  -->
        <!-- when this model is eventually wired into a controller (not V0).  -->
        <!-- ================================================================= -->
        <xacro:if value="${include_ros2_control}">
            <ros2_control name="${name}" type="system">
                <hardware>
                    <xacro:if value="${sim_isaac}">
                        <plugin>isaac_ros2_control/IsaacSystem</plugin>
                        <param name="joint_commands_topic">/isaac_joint_commands</param>
                        <param name="joint_states_topic">/isaac_joint_states</param>
                    </xacro:if>
                    <xacro:if value="${sim_ignition}">
                        <plugin>ign_ros2_control/IgnitionSystem</plugin>
                    </xacro:if>
                    <xacro:if value="${use_fake_hardware}">
                        <plugin>mock_components/GenericSystem</plugin>
                        <param name="fake_sensor_commands">${fake_sensor_commands}</param>
                        <param name="state_following_offset">0.0</param>
                    </xacro:if>
                </hardware>
                <joint name="${prefix}gripper_jaw_joint">
                    <command_interface name="position"/>
                    <command_interface name="effort"/>
                    <state_interface name="position">
                        <param name="initial_value">0.0</param>
                    </state_interface>
                    <state_interface name="velocity"/>
                    <state_interface name="effort"/>
                </joint>
            </ros2_control>
        </xacro:if>

        <!-- ================================================================= -->
        <!-- Links and joints                                                  -->
        <!-- ================================================================= -->
        <link name="${prefix}gripper_base_link">
            <!-- Visual-only placeholder box. No <collision>: this link must
                 never be able to touch anything (that is what removes defect 1,
                 the protruding-collider first-contact problem). -->
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <box size="0.030 0.060 0.030"/>
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
                <mass value="0.663"/>
                <inertia ixx="5.1617816e-04" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0"
                         iyy="5.8802208e-04" iyz="0.0" izz="3.9462776e-04"/>
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <joint name="${prefix}gripper_base_joint" type="fixed">
            <parent link="${parent}"/>
            <child link="${prefix}gripper_base_link"/>
            <xacro:insert_block name="origin"/>
        </joint>

        <!-- fixed jaw -->
        <link name="${prefix}jaw_fixed_link">
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
                <mass value="0.02"/>
                <inertia ixx="1.0e-6" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0"
                         iyy="1.0e-6" iyz="0.0" izz="1.0e-6"/>
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <joint name="${prefix}jaw_fixed_joint" type="fixed">
            <parent link="${prefix}gripper_base_link"/>
            <child link="${prefix}jaw_fixed_link"/>
            <origin xyz="${FIXED_JAW_X} 0 ${LZ}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        </joint>

        <link name="${prefix}pad_fixed_link">
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <box size="${pad_thickness_m} ${pad_width_m} ${pad_height_m}"/>
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <collision>
                <geometry>
                    <box size="${pad_thickness_m} ${pad_width_m} ${pad_height_m}"/>
                </geometry>
            </collision>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
                <mass value="0.01"/>
                <inertia ixx="1.0e-7" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0"
                         iyy="1.0e-7" iyz="0.0" izz="1.0e-7"/>
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <joint name="${prefix}pad_fixed_joint" type="fixed">
            <parent link="${prefix}jaw_fixed_link"/>
            <child link="${prefix}pad_fixed_link"/>
            <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        </joint>

        <!-- Friction/contact params carried over byte-identical from the
             vendor fingertip blocks (robotiq_2f_85_macro.urdf.xacro), see
             this file's header. Inline <surface> inside URDF <collision> is
             silently dropped by the URDF->SDF converter; this <gazebo
             reference> extension form is the one that survives, exactly as
             in the vendor macro. -->
        <gazebo reference="${prefix}pad_fixed_link">
            <collision>
                <surface>
                    <friction>
                        <ode>
                            <mu>100000.0</mu>
                            <mu2>100000.0</mu2>
                        </ode>
                    </friction>
                    <contact>
                        <ode>
                            <kp>1e+5</kp>
                            <kd>1</kd>
                            <soft_cfm>0</soft_cfm>
                            <soft_erp>0.2</soft_erp>
                            <min_depth>0.002</min_depth>
                            <max_vel>0</max_vel>
                        </ode>
                    </contact>
                </surface>
            </collision>
            <sensor name="${prefix}pad_fixed_contact" type="contact">
                <contact>
                    <collision>${prefix}pad_fixed_link_collision</collision>
                </contact>
                <update_rate>500</update_rate>
                <topic>${prefix}pad_fixed_link/contact</topic>
            </sensor>
        </gazebo>

        <!-- moving jaw — the ONE actuated DOF -->
        <link name="${prefix}jaw_moving_link">
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
                <mass value="0.02"/>
                <inertia ixx="1.0e-6" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0"
                         iyy="1.0e-6" iyz="0.0" izz="1.0e-6"/>
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <joint name="${prefix}gripper_jaw_joint" type="prismatic">
            <parent link="${prefix}gripper_base_link"/>
            <child link="${prefix}jaw_moving_link"/>
            <!-- axis -1 0 0: increasing q moves toward the fixed jaw (-X),
                 so aperture DECREASES with increasing q, same sign
                 convention as the vendor master joint (increasing angle ->
                 closing), per docs/GRIPPER_REDESIGN_DESIGN.md §3.2. -->
            <origin xyz="${MOVING_JAW_X0} 0 ${LZ}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
            <axis xyz="-1 0 0"/>
            <limit lower="0.0" upper="${A0}" velocity="${jaw_velocity}" effort="${jaw_effort}"/>
        </joint>

        <link name="${prefix}pad_moving_link">
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <box size="${pad_thickness_m} ${pad_width_m} ${pad_height_m}"/>
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <collision>
                <geometry>
                    <box size="${pad_thickness_m} ${pad_width_m} ${pad_height_m}"/>
                </geometry>
            </collision>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
                <mass value="0.01"/>
                <inertia ixx="1.0e-7" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0"
                         iyy="1.0e-7" iyz="0.0" izz="1.0e-7"/>
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <joint name="${prefix}pad_moving_joint" type="fixed">
            <parent link="${prefix}jaw_moving_link"/>
            <child link="${prefix}pad_moving_link"/>
            <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        </joint>

        <gazebo reference="${prefix}pad_moving_link">
            <collision>
                <surface>
                    <friction>
                        <ode>
                            <mu>100000.0</mu>
                            <mu2>100000.0</mu2>
                        </ode>
                    </friction>
                    <contact>
                        <ode>
                            <kp>1e+5</kp>
                            <kd>1</kd>
                            <soft_cfm>0</soft_cfm>
                            <soft_erp>0.2</soft_erp>
                            <min_depth>0.002</min_depth>
                            <max_vel>0</max_vel>
                        </ode>
                    </contact>
                </surface>
            </collision>
            <sensor name="${prefix}pad_moving_contact" type="contact">
                <contact>
                    <collision>${prefix}pad_moving_link_collision</collision>
                </contact>
                <update_rate>500</update_rate>
                <topic>${prefix}pad_moving_link/contact</topic>
            </sensor>
        </gazebo>

    </xacro:macro>
</robot>
